               was gradually expanded to persons aged $\geq$65 years beginning
               in January 2021. By April 19, 2021, eligibility was expanded to
               all adults aged $\geq$18 years nationwide.† To assess patterns
               of COVID-19 vaccination coverage among U.S. adults, CDC analyzed
               data submitted on vaccinations administered during December 14,
               2020-May 22, 2021, by age, sex, and community-level
               characteristics. By May 22, 2021, 57.0\% of persons aged
